1.What is Web Sever?
==================
A webserver handles:
-Static content
-Client request
-HTTP/HTTPS traffic
-Front delivery

Deliver web pages
It acts as the entry point for users.

Responsibilities:
------------------
-Serve HTML/CSS/JS/Images
-Reverse proxy request
-SSL termination
-Load balancing
-Caching

Real-Time Flow:
---------------
user request /open : https://amazon.com

Request first reaches to web servers:
Examples/name: 
1. NGINX : most popular modern web server
2. Apache : Traditional open source web server

Example:
--------
NGINX as Web Server

Internet User --> Nginx Web server --> Frontend files

what web server mainly Handles:
-------------------------------

Type:              Example:
----------------------------
Static Files       HTML
Images             PNG/JPG
CSS                Styling
Javascript         UI logic
SSL                HTTPS encryption


2.What is APP Server?
======================
An Application server handles:
-Business logic
-APIs (Application programming interface)
-Authentication
-Data processing
-Backend execution

Responsibilities:
-----------------
-Process API request
-Execute code
-Connect to database
-Handles business rules


Real-Time Example:
------------------
when user clicks:

"Place order"

Application server:
-Validates payment
-checks stock
-creates order
-sends confirmation

Popular App servers Example:
----------------------------
App server:          Used For:
-------------------------------
Apache tomcat        Java applications
JBoss EAP            Enterprise java apps
Node.js              Javascript backend

Example flow:
-------------
web server(nginx) ----> App server(tomcat/API)

Common backend technologies:
language:              Framework:
---------------------------------
Java                   Springboot
Python                 Flask/Django
Node.js                ExpressJS
.NET                   ASP.NET
Go                     Fiber


3.What is DB Server?
--------------------
A datbase server stores and manages data
It handles:
-data storage
-queries
-transaction
-backups

Responsibilities:
----------------
-store application data
-Run SQL queries
-Maintain consistency
-Handle transactions

Real-Time Example:
------------------
Amazon database stores:
-customer info
-orders
-payments
-product catalog

Popular database servers:
Datbase:              Type:
----------------------------
MySQL                 Relational DB
PostgreSQL            Advanced SQL DB
Oracle database       Enterprise DB
Mongo DB              document DB

datbase flow:
------------
APP server ----> MySQL/RDS DB server


Three Tier arhitecture:
----------------------
user Browser ---> WEB SERVER(NGINX/APACHE) ---> APP SERVER(Tomcat/NodeJS) ---> DATABASE Server(MySQL/Postgres)

Real-Time Example -- Banking Application:
==========================================
